#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
sdlc: the verification loop for this repository (PRD -> Code -> Test -> Deploy).

Standard library only (Python 3.9+). Configured by .ai/sdlc.json; see .ai/README.md.

  setup     install dependencies for every component
  doctor    check the toolchain this repo needs
  gates     run verification gates (lint, types, unit, build, contract, security)
  facts     check PRD acceptance criteria against the RUNNING system
  verify    gates + facts, one pass, no agent (this is what CI runs)
  loop      verify -> heal -> verify ... until green, stuck, or out of budget
  spec      draft prd.md + acceptance.json from a requirements document (PDF, DOCX, Markdown, text) with your agent
  implement turn a finished spec (prd.md + acceptance.json) into verified code with your agent
  agent     see which AI agents are installed and choose one (command-line agents, the Claude desktop app, a desktop app you drive, or your own)
  feature   drive one feature through PRD -> Code -> Test (-> Deploy)
  sync      install dependencies, only if the manifests changed since the last install
  onboard   adopted projects: an agent drafts a map of the repository and its conventions; the tool checks every path and command it cites
  baseline  adopted projects: record which gates pass today (--tighten locks in gates that now pass)
  new       create an empty feature spec from the template, by NAME (new user-login); for a document use `spec`
  deploy    deploy an image tag to an environment, then verify facts there
  secrets   scan the working tree for committed secrets
  up|down   start/stop the runtime used by facts
  report    print the latest evidence report

Exit codes: 0 ok | 1 verification failed | 2 needs a human | 3 no progress | 4 integrity violation
"""
